				<wikidot:authorName>Mark Penrice</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1858819</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Regarding aesthetics as mentioned by someone on page one of comments, whoever decided that the announcement colour scheme should include links in various shades of orange on top of a gradient medium light to medium dark beige background needs a shot in the head. It's almost completely unreadable, particularly for the lighter orange, even with full trichromacy. Any dichromats are going to have serious trouble.</p> <p>I mean, it's most likely just an accident, and I'm exaggerating for sarcastic humour reasons, but still&#8230; orange on brown in any case is a bad idea. Pls to feex.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-7733674#post-4045266</guid>
				<title>HAPPY HALLOWEEN! THE CONTEST IS CLOSED!</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-7733674/halloween-contest-2018#post-4045266</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 31 Oct 2018 04:46:36 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Dexanote</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>481882</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>AND WE HAVE ARRIVED.</p> <p>Today, on Halloween 2018 (Eastern Standard Time), the winner has been chosen.</p> <p>Congradulations to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rounderhouse" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4187885&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1540961280" alt="Rounderhouse" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4187885)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rounderhouse" >Rounderhouse</a></span>, and their tale <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/mtf-sigma-5-pumpkin-punchers">MTF Sigma-5: Pumpkin Punchers</a>, for taking first place with a whopping +97<a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-097">!</a>! You'll be contacted within the next few days for the prize.</p> <p>In second place, we have <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/uncle-nicolini" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3487700&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1540961280" alt="Uncle Nicolini" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3487700)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/uncle-nicolini" >Uncle Nicolini</a></span> gave us <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/moon-champion-s-cinco-de-mayo-extravaganza">Moon Champion's Cinco de Mayo Extravaganza</a>, at +84!</p> <p>In third, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gabriel-jade" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=414239&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1540961280" alt="Gabriel Jade" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=414239)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gabriel-jade" >Gabriel Jade</a></span> gave us <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/let-sleeping-dogs-lie-a-play-in-two-acts">Let Sleeping Dogs Lie, a Play In two Acts</a> at +64!</p> <p>Please, everybody, go and read all the entries today sometime. They’re all absolutely fantastic, and this was a very very good contest year. Happy Halloween!</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
