					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-7733674#post-4022358</guid>
				<title>STIPULATION UPDATE</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-7733674/halloween-contest-2018#post-4022358</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 12 Oct 2018 20:24:13 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Dexanote</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>481882</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The second stipulation has drawn a lot of private questions and grey scenarios for myself and Sly. Originally it read as such;</p> <blockquote> <p>&quot;No characters are allowed to acknowledge that it is in fact Halloween, but it must be blindingly obvious based on the setting.&quot;</p> </blockquote> <p>This was chosen as a storytelling restriction to encourage Show, Don't Tell. However&#8230;</p> <p>It's kind of confusing and people are having enough trouble that I have updated it for clarity and to better get across what we wanted out of this stipulation. It now reads&#8230;</p> <blockquote> <p>&quot;The piece itself cannot directly acknowledge that it is in fact Halloween, but it must be blindingly obvious based on the setting and storybuilding.&quot;</p> </blockquote> <p>People who have used this stipulation may make adjustments or leave their stories as they are, since it's been about a week before this edits gone into effect. Apologies for the clarity issues here; hope this helps!</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
